html='''<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>k-NN explanation selector</title><style>body{font:17px system-ui;max-width:1250px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 20px;color:#1b293a;line-height:1.55}img{width:100%}table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px}th,td{padding:7px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;text-align:right}th{background:#edf3f8}h2{margin-top:36px}.note{padding:18px;background:#edf3f8;border-radius:10px}</style></head><body><h1>k-NN with Euclidean and cosine distance</h1><div class="note">'''+headline+'''</div><img src="knn_comparison.png"><h2>What the distance measures</h2><p>This k-NN finds similar past validation examples of whether an NN explanation helped. It is separate from the neighbour retrieval used in the original prompt. Both distances operate on the same 31 standardized pre-judge features used by the previous classifier study: retrieval/probe statistics, known neighbour label and prediction, text overlap and lengths, dataset and backbone identity. These are not distances between raw text embeddings.</p><h2>Model selection</h2><p>We tested k=5,15,51,151 under both Euclidean and cosine distance. For each metric, k is chosen separately per original judge and threshold policy, using the same three target-grouped validation folds as before. Voting is weighted by the original cell-normalized inverse-inclusion sample weights; we do not additionally inverse-distance-weight votes. Standardization is fitted inside each training fold. k is capped to the available training disagreements if necessary; a single-class or empty training set gives a constant score.</p><p>Gate cutoffs are chosen per judge/backbone/dataset from out-of-fold validation scores by F1, with always/never endpoints. Validation-selected k-NN chooses the metric and k without looking at test. Expanded CV selection also compares with the original logistic/tree candidates using their saved validation scores. Original results and models remain unchanged. All choices are saved before any new test evaluation.</p><h2>Fixed50 metrics</h2><p>Percentages, averaged equally across500 original judge/backbone/dataset combinations.</p>'''+table(q[q.policy=='fixed50'][['method','f1','precision','recall','accuracy','nn_rate']])+'''<h2>Shared tuned thresholds</h2>'''+table(q[q.policy=='anchor_average'][['method','f1','precision','recall','accuracy','nn_rate']])+'''<h2>Fixed50 F1 by outcome judge</h2>'''+table(j.reset_index())+'''<h2>Choices made using validation</h2>'''+table(sel.reset_index())+'''<h2>Limits and artifacts</h2><p>This is another exploratory comparison on the previously inspected test set. Results are point estimates; model search is larger than the original logistic/tree search. Numerical differences between test families do not establish which is universally best. No new LLM calls, target gold labels as input, or test-only mechanism annotations were used. Original inference settings, weights and held-out memberships are unchanged.</p><ul>'''+''.join('<li><a href="'+x+'">'+x+'</a></li>' for x in ['summary.csv','deltas.csv','all_cell_metrics.csv','validation_candidates.csv','validation_cutoffs.csv','model_choices.csv','test_predictions.csv.gz','SELECTION_FROZEN.json','COMPLETED.json','knn_comparison.pdf'])+'''</ul><p><a href="../../nn_learned_gate_20261019/results/report.html">Original logistic/tree experiment</a></p></body></html>'''
